# Print-in-place fit proofs for the chain run. The `fitcheck` family guards
# the print pose: every adjacent link pair must overlap NOWHERE (zero facets)
# — the pin stubs ride their bores, lugs clear ears, plates clear lugs.
# `fitcheck_neg` proves the check can fail: an oversized stub in link 0 MUST
# overlap link 1's ears (a welded stub is exactly what a 100/100 watertight
# score cannot see). The `pose_*`/`stop_*` pairs prove the articulation and
# the end stops at BOTH sweep limits: 1° short of the ±45° stop must clear
# (EMPTY) — the joint really articulates through its range — and 2° past must
# interfere (NON-EMPTY) — the printed plate stops are what block it, at the
# angle the derivation claims. `tab-wall` / `tab-wall-neg` gate the last
# link's front M4 mounting tab: the 0.8 mm annulus around the Ø4.5 clearance
# hole minus the printed tab must be EMPTY (≥0.8 mm of plastic all around —
# the #717 defect left only 0.23 mm outboard and no gate saw it), and the
# same probe at 3 mm MUST leave leftover (the check can still fail). All
# eight are rendered straight from the production link(); none is posed by
# hand.
fitcheck      empty
fitcheck_neg  interferes
pose_up44     empty
pose_dn44     empty
stop_up47     interferes
stop_dn47     interferes
tab-wall      empty
tab-wall-neg  interferes
